id: pm-7km8
title: Upstream template SDK loses own keys and inherits phantom builtin names
description: "Observed with @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.25: a valid user template containing an own __proto__ string option survives in stored JSON, but loadCreateTemplateOptions and runTemplatesShow return success while omitting that option. An ordinary option and constructor option survive. The upstream template parser and flag extractor clone arbitrary keys onto ordinary objects through indexed assignment. This is outside the pm-presets implementation; PR #170 preserves its own JSON dictionaries and refuses unsupported public-document keys and partial native projections until the host supports them safely."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: host-sdk,own-keys,templates,upstream
created_at: "2026-10-29T07:06:09.014Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-31T02:59:30.379Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-31T02:59:29.453Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-31T02:15:17.000Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: "Add adversarial own-key properties for SDK template parse/save/show and real CLI JSON/TOON, including Object.prototype names and prototype integrity on nongit trackers. Preserve expected SDK error identity. Revisit the pm-presets compatibility refusals after supported host versions preserve these keys."
repro_steps: "Initialize a scratch tracker using PmClient with noExtensions. Write templates/own-key.json using JSON.parse for {\"name\":\"own-key\",\"options\":{\"__proto__\":\"public-data\",\"ordinary\":\"kept\",\"constructor\":\"kept\"}}. Call loadCreateTemplateOptions and runTemplatesShow through the pinned SDK. Both successful results omit __proto__ although the stored file retains the field. All data is synthetic."
resolution: "Delivered by PR #170 (a9d3827): Typed parameter binding manifests: declare preset parameters once, resolve across settings, templates and seeds"
expected_result: "Preserve every accepted option as an own data property, or return a typed refusal before accepting/writing unsupported input. Never change prototypes or silently produce partial data."
actual_result: Both SDK reads omit __proto__; ordinary and constructor controls remain. SDK source confirms unsafe indexed assignment in template option cloning.
affected_version: 2026.10.25
component: upstream template SDK
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T07:19:27.672Z",codex-sol,Confirmed against the pinned 2026.10.25 SDK using synthetic user-template JSON. The package compatibility tests now require explicit refusal for unsupported public-document fields before writes and for partial legacy projections before output/export. The SDK parser/flag-extractor fix remains upstream work; this follow-up stays open and unclaimed. No private data or tracker history was rewritten.
  "2026-10-29T08:14:04.385Z",codex-sol,"Additional host compatibility evidence: audited settings callbacks project only native fields, so package merges preserve extension fields from the locked raw snapshot. The host intentionally rejects nested __proto__ JSON-Patch edits; the package now emits typed preflight/locked refusals instead of relying on that generic audit failure. This follow-up remains focused on silent SDK template option loss; do not disable host prototype protections."
  "2026-10-29T08:32:19.068Z",codex-sol,"Confirmed the related builtin lookup defect with an isolated SDK workspace: constructor-like inherited names resolve successfully as phantom builtins even though the native inventory omits them. The package adapter now verifies builtin results against the own SDK inventory and still accepts a real user template named constructor. Removing that guard fails the new missing-refusal property. Upstream acceptance should cover own-key cloning and own inventory membership together, preserving native expected errors."
  "2026-10-29T18:02:56.796Z",codex-agent,"Additional evidence for the upstream own-property lookup class: the pinned public resolveTypeSynonym('constructor') returns an inherited function instead of its declared string-or-undefined result. The package seed normalizer now checks the return type and uses own-entry lookups before applying any synonym; an adversarial constructor case covers it. This is a host implementation bug, not a missing SDK signature; no upstream repository changes were made."
